Present the MiniLoong Pocket1 pad as a GO-Super Gamepad.

AmberELEC's controller configs - SDL game controller mappings, RetroArch
autoconfig, EmulationStation, the standalone emulators and the hotkey
scripts - are written for the RG552's pad, "GO-Super Gamepad", which uses the
same singleadc-joypad driver. A pad that reports the same name, product ID and
button indexes gets all of them without any per-device configuration.

This board reported itself as "retrogame_joypad" (product 0x1101) and used
BTN_SELECT/BTN_START/BTN_THUMBL/BTN_MODE where the GO-Super pad has F1-F5
(BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1-5). SDL numbers buttons by the codes present, so every
index after R2 was shifted and standalone emulators had no mapping at all.

Match the node name, joypad-name, product and codes: select -> F1, start ->
F2, L3 -> F3, MODE -> F5. The board has no right-stick click (F4), so advertise
that code as a placeholder (see the singleadcjoy placeholder-codes patch) to
keep MODE on F5's index. The face buttons, shoulders, D-pad and stick already
matched.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miniloong.dts	2026-09-27 18:53:30.797505049 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miniloong.dts	2026-09-27 19:26:38.644330823 +0200
@@ -243,7 +243,7 @@
 		};
 	};
 	
-	joypad: singleadc-joypad {
+	joypad: odroidgo3-joypad {
 		/*
 		 * Requires patched singleadcjoy.c with Miniloong direct-adc mode.
 		 *
@@ -266,8 +266,14 @@
 		/* pwms = <&pwm5 0 10000 0>; */
 		pwms = <&pwm2 0 10000 0>;
 
-		joypad-name = "retrogame_joypad";
-		joypad-product = <0x1101>;
+		joypad-name = "GO-Super Gamepad";
+		joypad-product = <0x1100>;
+		/*
+		 * The GO-Super layout has a right-stick click (F4) this board
+		 * lacks. Advertise its code with no GPIO behind it so MODE lands
+		 * on F5's index like on the RG552, not on F4's.
+		 */
+		linux,placeholder-codes = <BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY4>;
 		joypad-revision = <0x0100>;
 
 		/*
@@ -355,19 +361,19 @@
 		sw9 {
 			gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			label = "SELECT";
-			linux,code = <BTN_SELECT>;
+			linux,code = <BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1>;
 		};
 
 		sw10 {
 			gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			label = "START";
-			linux,code = <BTN_START>;
+			linux,code = <BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY2>;
 		};
 
 		sw11 {
 			gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			label = "MODE";
-			linux,code = <BTN_MODE>;
+			linux,code = <BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY5>;
 		};
 
 		sw12 {
@@ -397,7 +403,7 @@
 		sw16 {
 			gpios = <&gpio2 RK_PC5 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			label = "LEFT JOYSTICK MIDDLE";
-			linux,code = <BTN_THUMBL>;
+			linux,code = <BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY3>;
 		};
 	};
 
